# Composition and type induction

r1, 2026-11-03. **Draft, awaiting plan review and the owner's plan gate.**
Milestone: `composition-and-type-induction`.
Sources: [issue #73](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/73) (GR-T10),
[#77](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/77) (GR-T14), and the
owner's direction of 2026-11-03 to plan them as the successor of
[model-growth-guardrails](../../model-growth-guardrails/notes/model-growth-guardrails-plan.md).
Inspection baseline: `1446f90` (main after PR #79).
Plan authorship is not approval. No phase has a spec approval; no code is
written. CT4 is blocked until MG2 and MG3 merge.

**Owner rulings.** `(o1)` 2026-11-03, recorded in the predecessor plan's
header, rules CT-D1 (a): four local readers for plan review, provisional for
the close review until confirmed at the plan gate. It approves no bytes.

## Problem and completion predicates

**Composition (#73).** An anchor sidecar binds one population to one
document: it carries the raw-byte SHA-256 of each (`anchors.py:48-54,228`),
and `gnd check --anchors --document` checks each anchored value against its
span. A downstream application extracts facts per document, then needs one
population per task, built from many documents, to evaluate derivation rules
over. Merging changes the population digest and can change fact keys, so the
sidecars stop binding, and the application keeps its own provenance map that
GND cannot check. It also needs several spans for one fact role (a definition
and the clause that uses it); the parser refuses that today
(`anchors.py:133-135`), and the checker keeps only the last record per key
(`checker/_core.py:1911-1917`).

**Type induction (#77).** `gnd discover` proposes constraints of seven
families, as an evolve proposal for review. When facts land in a generic fact
type ("entity has attribute with value"), a recurring attribute name with a
consistent value type often calls for a dedicated fact type. Nothing proposes
that today. It is the type-level part of the closed
[issue #34](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/34).

The milestone can close when:

1. A version-2 sidecar may hold several anchors for one fact role; `gnd check`
   evaluates `anchored` constraints over all of them under the CT-D2 rule;
   every version-1 sidecar checks exactly as at `1446f90` (CT1).
2. `gnd compose` and `gnd.api.compose` build one population from several
   (document, population, sidecar) inputs and an explicit transformation
   manifest, and write a composition record GND can check. `gnd check
   --composition` re-verifies every source binding and every composed fact's
   lineage, and refuses a record whose bytes or lineage differ (CT2).
3. A derivation witness over a composed population names, for each base
   fact, its source facts, and through their sidecars their document spans;
   `gnd replay` verifies that lineage (CT3).
4. `gnd discover --families fact-type` proposes dedicated fact types from a
   generic fact type's rows, above a stated support threshold, as an
   additive, `proposed`, `deontic` evolve proposal plus a migration report of
   opaque row ids. The proposal passes `gnd evolve preview --policy
   additive`, and each proposal carries its MG3 shape matches (CT4).
5. Docs dispositions recorded, new pages executed, docs gates exit 0 (CT5).
6. Focused gates, independent diff reviews, the question sweep and a PR are
   recorded. Owner acceptance is separate.

## 0. Binding design rules

| Rule | Requirement |
|---|---|
| CT-R1: Old artifacts keep their meaning | Version-1 sidecars, witnesses without composition, discover runs without the new family, and evolve proposals at schema 3 parse, check and replay byte-identically to `1446f90`. |
| CT-R2: Anchors bind values to ranges, nothing more | Neither GND nor the caller claims that a span entails a fact (issue #73's own boundary). Several anchors add evidence for one role; none of them proves the fact. Docs say so. |
| CT-R3: Composition is explicit and checkable | Every change composition makes (deduplication, renaming, scope tag) is listed in a caller-supplied manifest. GND never infers a merge. The composition record binds every input by digest and every composed fact to its source facts; a checker re-derives the composed population from the inputs and the manifest and compares bytes. |
| CT-R4: Digests are defined over stated bytes | Each new digest names its input: raw bytes for files a caller writes (sidecars, documents, populations, as today), canonical JSON for records GND writes. The canonical form is the existing helper, not a second implementation (standing rules, "interchange field"). |
| CT-R5: Induction proposes; review admits | The type family emits `source: induced`, `status: proposed`, `modality: deontic` on everything it proposes, and never deletes or moves rows. Admission is a reviewed `gnd evolve` apply. |
| CT-R6: No population value becomes a model name without a ruling | A proposed fact type's id and reading derive from an attribute-name value only as CT-D9 rules; redacted roles never contribute (owner ruling 2026-10-25, `discover/candidates.py:131-132`). |
| CT-R7: Disclosure | New CLI leaves and API callables get rows in `gnd.disclosure`'s total table. Composition records and witnesses carry population values the way check-family outputs do and follow the mode the same way. Discover keeps its every-mode row (NM-D13). |
| CT-R8: Layering, query policy, anonymity, approval | As MG-R6 and MG-R7 of the predecessor. The composer lives at layer `model` beside `bind_population`; composed-anchor checking at `checking`; API wrappers at `entry`. `auto=false`. |

Each phase spec binds every rule above and every rule in
`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/standing-rules.md`, by name or with a
one-sentence argument that it does not apply.

