## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces

- New: sidecar v2; a published sidecar schema; two composition schemas; one
  CLI leaf (`gnd compose`) and options on `check` and `replay`; one API
  callable and one keyword; witness fields; one discover family and options.
- **Unchanged without the new inputs:** v1 sidecars, check, witness, replay
  and discover outputs (CT-R1). Root help and RF1 goldens change for the new
  leaf and options; `gnd.api.__all__` grows by one name; the discover help
  "seven" wording changes to name the opt-in family.
- Packaged skills: `gnd-extract` (sidecar v2), `gnd-orm-core` constraint
  reference (anchored with several anchors), and the discover sections that
  mention families. Twins kept byte-identical.

## 6. Risks and required controls

| Risk | Control |
|---|---|
| Several anchors read as stronger proof | CT-R2 in docs; CT-D2 names exactly what passes |
| Composition silently merges distinct entities | CT-R3: only manifest renamings change values; dedupe only of identical rows by default |
| A composed population drifts from its sources | Checker re-derives and compares bytes |
| Two digest forms confused | CT-R4: each digest names its bytes; one canonical helper |
| Witness format breaks old replays | CT-R1; CT3-C1 v1 parity |
| Type proposals leak population values into model names | CT-R6; CT-D9 |
| Induction proposes a duplicate of an existing type | MG3 shape check before proposing |
| Rows moved without review | CT-R5: report only, nothing moves |
| Prerequisite milestone slips | CT4 blocked explicitly; CT1–CT3 proceed |
| Downstream names leak | CT-R8 |

## 7. Out of scope

- Inferring merges, entity resolution, fuzzy matching across documents.
- Anchors combined with reference populations (still refused,
  `checking_service.py:222-223`), unless CT-D11 rules otherwise.
- Moving rows into proposed fact types; any non-additive evolve operation.
- Structural detection of generic fact types.
- Constraint induction on the newly proposed fact types beyond the one
  uniqueness carrying the envelope.
- Publication, release, certification.

## 8. Execution, approval and review protocol

As the predecessor's §8: `auto=false`, `process-phase` per phase, no code
before recorded spec approval, plan and close review per CT-D1, at most two
plan review rounds with the stop rule declared here, topic branch and PR,
merge by the owner.

## 9. Per-phase verification story

| Phase | Expected result | Focused gate |
|---|---|---|
| CT1 | v2 parse and check; v1 parity | `uv run pytest -q` over the anchor, checker-anchored, verbalize-population and export-verification test files (exact list fixed in the CT1 spec) plus a new `tests/test_anchor_sidecar_v2.py` |
| CT2 | Compose, re-derive, refuse | CT1 gate plus `tests/test_composition.py`, public API pins, RF1 CLI pins, disclosure table |
| CT3 | Lineage in witness and replay; v1 replay parity | CT2 gate plus the witness and replay test files and a new `tests/test_witness_composition.py` |
| CT4 | Family proposals; additive pass; parity | discover test files, `tests/test_discover_fact_type_family.py`, the MG2 policy tests |
| CT5 | Pages executed; checkpoints seen | `tools/run_tutorials.py`, `zensical build --strict`, `tools/check_docs.py site` |

## 10. Owner decisions and open questions

| ID | Question | Readings and cost | Proposal |
|---|---|---|---|
| CT-D1 | Plan and close review instrument | (a) four local readers; (b) six-seat panel | **Ruled `(o1)`: (a)** for plan review; close review confirmed at the plan gate |
| CT-D2 | When does a role with several anchors pass `anchored`? | (a) every anchor binds its value within its span: each anchor is a claim and a false one is an error; (b) any one anchor binds: one good anchor hides a wrong one | (a) |
| CT-D3 | Deduplication | (a) identical rows (same fact type, same role values after renaming) collapse into one composed fact with all their source facts as lineage; (b) no dedupe, keep every row: functional constraints then fail on harmless repeats | (a) |
| CT-D4 | Conflicting functional values across sources | (a) refuse the composition (exit 3) naming both source facts; (b) compose and let `gnd check` report the uniqueness violation: the conflict is real data and the check reports it with lineage | (b): composition is not a constraint checker; the record's lineage makes the check's report traceable |
| CT-D5 | Where scope tags live | (a) in the composition record only; (b) as a role in the composed population: changes fact shapes, breaks the model | (a) |
| CT-D6 | Witness lineage shape | (a) keep `origin.kind: candidate`, add `sources`; (b) a new `origin.kind: source`: the kernel would resolve rows in sources, a larger change | (a) |
| CT-D7 | How a generic fact type is identified | (a) declared in `provenance.generic`; (b) structural guess (arity 3, two value roles): false positives become model proposals | (a) |
| CT-D8 | Where the induced envelope sits | (a) on a uniqueness constraint the proposal adds; (b) a schema change giving fact types `source`/`status`/`modality`: model-spec change across validation and evolve | (a) |
| CT-D9 | Naming a proposed fact type from an attribute value | (a) id `ft_<generic id>_<slug of value>`, reading `"<Entity> has <value> <ValueType>"`, only for unredacted roles, documented as a disclosure of that value into the model; (b) an opaque id plus the value only in the migration report, so a reviewer names it: no value in the model until a human picks a name | (b) |
| CT-D10 | Support threshold | (a) `--min-support N` (distinct entities), default 20, no admission by `check` verdict for this family; (b) a fraction of entities: unstable on small populations | (a) |
| CT-D11 | Composition with reference populations | (a) stays refused this milestone; (b) supported: reopens the anchors-with-references refusal | (a) |
| CT-D12 | Sidecar version for multi-document | (a) composition keeps one document per sidecar (v2 is about several anchors only); (b) v2 also allows several documents per sidecar: two ways to say the same thing | (a) |

